    "notes": "Closed score labelled only \"S A\" and \"T B\". mm.1-2: soprano and alto sing the same notes (every head carries an up- and a down-stem) - both parts get the full phrase. m.4-5: the soprano g' is TIED over the barline while the alto RE-ATTACKS g' on m.5 beat 1 (same head position): truth has a tie in Soprano and a new note in Alto; the same happens in mm.7-8 on the bass staff (tenor a tied, bass re-attacks a). mm.5-6: upper voices and tenor rest while the bass sings a solo whose words (\"Peace on earth, and mercy mild\") are printed under the bass staff and belong to the Bass. m.7: alto enters after a quarter rest. Amen (mm.9-10): the soprano sings two-note chords on its up-stem and the bass octaves on its down-stem - these must stay chords inside Soprano/Bass (must_not_split refers to these chords), the alto and tenor single notes are separate parts. Exactly 4 parts."
  },
